PICONIX SHELL SYNTAX (NOT BASH)

Interactive sh: finite single command lines, optional simple pipelines
(up to three stages), and file redirections <, >, >>.
A trailing & requests background execution in the interactive shell.
MCP execute_command runs sh -c: ANY '&' character is rejected,
including && (the rejection text is 'background disabled').
Do not use &&, ||, ;, command substitution, $VAR expansion,
globbing, or 2>&1 as if this were bash.

To run steps with MCP, issue separate execute_command calls,
inspect each result before continuing, and do not spawn jobs.
A literal '||' may be interpreted as pipes, not boolean OR.
'/' in paths and '-' in command options are NOT shell operators.
Command options are app-specific: use help COMMAND.
